        "og:description": "The concept of a judgment as a logical action which introduces new information into a deductive system is examined. This leads to a way of mathematically representing implication which is distinct from the familiar material implication, according to which \"If A then B\" is considered to be equivalent to \"B or not-A\". This leads, in turn, to a resolution of the paradox of the raven.",
